.LONG TERM...
Issued at 125 PM PDT Thu Aug 27 2026
(Saturday through next Wednesday)

A reinforcing trough deepens off of the Pacific Northwest coast by
Monday, allowing afternoon temperatures to be some 5 to 15 degrees
below seasonal averages. The current forecast has the potential for
rain showers returning towards the middle of next week. However, the
evolution of things across the tropical Eastern Pacific remains in
question, mainly in the form of remnant tropical moisture to be
pulled in from the south. Thus, forecast confidence remains low at
this time.

