.AVIATION...
(00Z TAFS)
Issued at 557 PM PDT Thu Aug 27 2026

It`s VFR with widespread mid and high level clouds over much of
the forecast area. There are high based showers as well. A few
showers have been reaching the ground over the north Central Coast
based on webcam and spotter reports. Increased cloud cover i.e.
water vapor will interfere with and decrease radiative cooling;
coastal stratus and fog will be limited tonight and Friday.

It`s a complex forecast over the next 12-24 hours. Subtropical jet
stream winds and upper level divergence are aligned with the current
water vapor plume with a 700 mb to 500 mb shortwave trough arriving
from the southwest Friday morning. Stay tuned to the latest updates.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. A few showers are possible tonight and/or
Friday. Currently, the 00z TAF advertises vicinity showers (VCSH)
11z-20z Friday. West to northwest wind 8 to 14 knots.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Vicinity showers (VCSH) tonight, with
tempo showers 10z-15z Friday morning and showers prevailing until
late Friday morning at the terminals. Winds will be a mix of west to
northwest 5 to 15 knots and light and variable.

