.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 125 PM PDT Thu Aug 27 2026

One more day of near-critical fire weather conditions above 1000
feet, especially across the Central Coast, as warm and dry
conditions continue above the marine layer inversion and overnight
humidity recoveries remain poor into Friday morning. There still is
a non-zero chance for thunderstorms across the Central Coast today
through tonight. By tomorrow, with the increasing potential for
lightning, we have issued a Red Flag Warning for much of the Central
Coast including the Santa Cruz Mountains from 5 AM to 3 PM Friday
given the low confidence for wetting rains to develop. By Friday
night and into the weekend, the cooling trend will continue and
bring cooler temperatures and likely a deeper marine layer, bringing
progressively more relief to some of the higher elevations.

